		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Help picking which rigid body library to use]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=27787#p27787"><![CDATA[
AGX Multiphysics has the functionality you need. In particular, if your system is stiff (e.g. high tension in the wires and/or large mass ratios), then I doubt that the game engines will be of much use. They can deal with ratios of perhaps 1:50 while AGX can handle 1:1e9 in such cases, with retained physical parameters for e.g. elasticity. See: <a href="http://www.algoryx.se/" class="postlink">http://www.algoryx.se/</a><br>Also see some of the research background: <a href="http://www.physics.umu.se/english/research/statistical-physics-and-networks/complex-mechanical-systems/realtime-wire-simulation/" class="postlink">http://www.physics.umu.se/english/resea ... imulation/</a><br><br>/Kenneth<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1339">KenB</a> — Mon May 07, 2012 9:03 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
